stanzaFirst = \lyricmode {
  \small \skip1*3 |

  \set stanza = "1. "
  \skip2.  I8 was |
  sit-8 ting by a riv- er when the | thought8 oc- curred to me
  There are a | hun-8 dred thou- sand riv- ers that we | ne-8 ver e- ven see
  They are the | bound-8 a- ries of all we know of | truth8 and right and wrong
  And I have | writ-8 ten some ex- am- ples for you | here8 with- in my song4
  Some8 are | bridged8 and some are for- ded some are | swol-8 len from the rains
  Some are the | ul-8 ti- mate re- sult of all our | joy8 and all our pains
  But when the | riv-8 ers of your life are full and | star-8 ting to wash down4
  You've8 got16 to | drink4 up8 the riv-4 er8 be- | fore4 you drown

  % Chorus
  You've8 got16 to | drink4 up8 the riv- er
  You've8 got16 to | drink4 up8 the riv- er
  You've8 got16 to | drink4 up8 the riv-4 er8 be- | fore4 you drown
  You've8 got16 to | drink4 up8 the riv- er
  You've8 got16 to | drink4 up8 the riv- er
  You've8 got16 to | drink4 up8 the riv-4 er8 be- | fore4 you drown2
  \skip1 |
  \time 2/4
  \set stanza = "2. "
  And4 all |
